From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:59:08 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] fds-bios

Before a disk starts slot checks BIOS/disksys.rom: present, 8192 bytes,
crc32 0x5e607dcf (the disksys.rom row of libretro-database
dat/System.dat, md5 ca30b50f880eb660a320674ed365ef7a). Missing or the
wrong size: the disk stays on the shelf with "FDS needs
BIOS/disksys.rom", because fceumm refuses a disk without it. Another
8 KB file launches with one "disksys.rom is not the known dump" toast a
session. A disk resumed at boot is checked the same way. The toasts,
and the eight side banners the disk control shows, upload after the
arcade one.
